math_notes.steepest_descent_quadratic:
Gradient descent specialized to a quadratic objective \( f(x)=	frac{1}{2}x^TQx-b^Tx \) (so \( 
abla f(x) = Qx-b \)) with the EXACT optimal step size at each iteration in closed form, \( \alpha_k = \dfrac{
abla f(x_k)^T 
abla f(x_k)}{
abla f(x_k)^T Q 
abla f(x_k)} \), rather than a line search -- converges to the same answer `quadratic_minimize` gives directly, but iteratively; useful when \( Q \) is too large or ill-conditioned to solve directly.
